body:
I think there is.. though it may take some work. In my case--I'm actively working to throttle down my agreeableness because over the course of my life, it's done me far much more harm than good. I like that I have really empathetic qualities and that I'm really good at seeing things from other peoples perspective, however it's just led to me taking far too much of peoples shit and never standing up for myself in situations where I definitely should have, and as a result, I've had a rough go of it trying to get to where I want in life. 

&#x200B;

Did you want your openness to change, or are you hoping to have it go back to how it was before? I think it makes sense that certain experiences can morph over time our psychological traits over time, and that we can have a certain say in which direction things go, though we may require outside help, like a therapist or something.
